# LF everywhere, on every checkout. A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand
# CRLF templates to the engine, which copies them byte-for-byte into every project (and bash
# chokes on a CRLF .sh). PowerShell reads LF scripts fine. tests/lint-skills.py enforces this.
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe misreads labels and long lines in an LF batch file.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
